  "status": "Refused",
  "actual_commencement_date": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;Furthermore the proposed development fails to provide a scheme which protects and enhances biodiversity in terms of future-proofing the development and its longer-term impacts on the natural environment. It would create a longer-term reliance on maintenance and site management in order to achieve a successful landscaping scheme, which is considered harmful to the natural environment and is contrary to the aims of Policy 79 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed residential accommodation, by virtue of its siting, fails to integrate successfully with the general character of Sopwith Avenue. The lack of separation between the four residential units, footpath, vehicle parking spaces and the public highway would mean for a contrived layout which does not fully relate to the character and appearance of Sopwith Avenue. This is therefore considered harmful to the overall character and appearance of the streetscene and is contrary to the objectives of Policy 53 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed intensification of the outdoor courtyard amenity space would mean that occupiers of any adjacent habitable rooms may be significantly compromised. The unrestricted use would create a sense of enclosure which is to the detriment of continued enjoyment of these habitable rooms, which is contrary to the aims and objectives of Policy 57 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement, the proposal fails to provide the necessary financial contributions to secure adequate mitigation against the Epping Forest Special Area of Conservation and therefore fails to comply with Policy 81 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
